== Absolute Value

=== Definition

The absolute value of $x$, denoted by $|x|$ is defined by:

$ |x| = cases(
  x quad "if" x >= 0,
  -x quad "if" x < 0
) $

=== Properties and Theorems

$ |x| < a <==> -a < x < a, quad "where" a > 0 $

$ |x| <= a <==> -a <= x <= a, quad "where" a > 0 $

$ |x| > a <==> (x > a) or (x < -a), quad "where" a > 0 $

$ |x| >= a <==> (x >= a) or (x <= -a), quad "where" a > 0 $

$ |a b| = |a| dot |b|, quad "where" a, b in RR $

$ lr(|a/b|) = (|a|)/(|b|), quad "where" a, b in RR, "and" b != 0 $

$ |a + b| <= |a| + |b|, quad "where" a, b in RR $

$ |a - b| <= |a| + |b|, quad "where" a, b in RR $

$ |a| - |b| <= |a - b|, quad "where" a, b in RR $
